{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>I, I am your comforter.</b> A sign for the prophet to Israel." "<b>Who are you.</b> According to everyone, He speaks to Israel, but in my opinion the prophet speaks in the holy spirit with his own soul, and the proof is \"and I have put My words in your mouth\" (Isaiah 51:16)." "<b>Grass.</b> Defective [spelling] of vav, like אש אוכלה הוא (Deuteronomy 4:24)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:59.973273130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}